    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/rbmor/ontologies/2021/1/1/untitled-ontology-133#12_to_13">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/rbmor/ontologies/2021/1/1/untitled-ontology-133#Edinburgh_Perinatal_Postnatal_Depression_Scale_Score"/>
        <rdfs:comment>High possibility of postpartum depression diagnosis.

http://www.perinatalservicesbc.ca/health-professionals/professional-resources/health-promo/edinburgh-postnatal-depression-scale-(epds)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>The cutoff of 12 or 13 is recommended to avoid over-inclusiveness caused by a cutoff of 9 or 10.

Cox J, Holden J, Henshaw C, editors. Perinatal Mental Health: the Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS) manual. 2nd edn. London: RCPsch Publications; 2014</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


